# Studio UI Rules

## Deck System
- Deck 0 = Effects (bridge-native: candle, fire, sparkle, etc.)
- Deck 1 = Live Modes (app-driven: strobe, party, thunderstorm, ambient)
- Deck 2 = Composer (composition presets + "+ Create" button) — SHIPPED; do not rebuild it

## Card Grid Pattern
Cards use `StudioCard` struct with: id, name, tagline, icon, accentColor, strategy.
Composer cards come from `vm.composerStudioCards` (computed from `CompositionStore`).

## Customization Host Pattern
- The host is `StudioCustomizationHost`, which lives in `MixerTrayView.swift`
  (the FILE rename is a queued `project.pbxproj` chore; there is no
  `MixerTrayView` type)
- `StudioView` mounts it INLINE when `vm.currentRoomEffect != nil` and the
  region mode is `.customization`; the deck pager is unmounted in that mode
- It is NOT a slide-up tray: no bottom-anchored overlay, no scrim, no fixed
  height. One vertical scroll surface with a pinned header (the quiet identity
  line + "Back to decks")
- Content is the per-look `StudioBoardView(card:effect:vm:)` for engine/effect
  cards, or `CompositionEditorPanel` for compositions
- Compositions keep the 4 layer tabs (`CompositionLayerTab`: palette, motion,
  envelope, reaction) and the save action

## Running State
- `vm.runningCardID` — which card shows as "running" on current room
- `vm.currentRoomEffect` — `runningEffects[StudioSelectionKey(room:)]` for the selected room: an EXACT bridge + group + kind lookup, never a bare room-id match
- `vm.hasAnyRunningEffect` — any room running anything
- Card grid shows pulse animation on running card

## Design Tokens
- Background: `HuePalette.Noir.background`
- Cards: `HuePalette.Noir.card`
- Accent: card's own `accentColor`
- Typography: `HueTypography.caption`, `.body`, `.title3`
- Corner radius: 16 for cards, 20 for sheets
- Glassmorphism: `.ultraThinMaterial` backgrounds
